# Blocked Binary Notifier Deployment Script

## Overview

This deployment script installs, configures and protects a macOS security notification framework that monitors Apple's **LaunchPolicy Endpoint Security** events generated by `managedeventsd`.

When a managed binary execution control policy denies an application launch, the framework displays a user-friendly swiftDialog notification containing application identity information extracted from code-signing metadata.

The deployment consists of:

1. Blocked Binary Notifier Script
2. Notifier LaunchDaemon
3. Watchdog Script
4. Watchdog LaunchDaemon
5. File Hardening
6. LaunchDaemon Self-Healing
7. Duplicate Event Suppression
8. Application Metadata Collection
9. swiftDialog User Notifications

---

# Deployment Components

| Component | Purpose |
|------------|------------|
| blocked-binary-notifier.sh | Monitors LaunchPolicy DENIED events |
| com.security.mac.blocked-binary-notifier.plist | Runs notifier continuously |
| blocked-binary-notifier-watchdog.sh | Protects and validates deployment |
| com.security.mac.blocked-binary-notifier-watchdog.plist | Executes watchdog every 60 seconds |

---

# Event Source

The notifier watches:

```text
com.apple.devicemanagementclient.managedeventsd
```

Category:

```text
LaunchPolicy
```

Expected event format:

```text
DENIED exec: pid 44526, path /Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome
```

Only launch events containing:

```text
DENIED exec:
```

are processed.

Other denied events are ignored.

